# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — the PUBLISH BOUNDARY in image form (O72)
# =============================================================================
# CLAUDE.md §3 keeps Internal material out of a public push. An image is the
# other way the same material leaves the machine: a `COPY . .` bakes whatever is
# in the build context into a layer, where it survives every later `rm` and
# travels with the image. So the rule that decides what may be pushed to GitHub
# decides what may enter a build context, and this file is where that is said.
#
# Read it as three groups, most important first.

# ---- 1. NEVER BAKED: secrets and Internal material --------------------------
# internal-local/ holds console-credentials.json (scrypt hashes of the console
# secrets). The API still reads it in the stack — as a READ-ONLY BIND MOUNT at
# run time (see compose.yaml), which is the point of excluding it here: the
# secret reaches the running container and never the image.
internal-local/
internal/
# .env* is gitignored for the same reason (root, agents/, web/) — Neo4j and
# provider credentials. Compose passes what a service needs as environment.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# ---- 2. CORRECTNESS: host state that must not leak into a build -------------
# node_modules is platform-specific — a Windows tree copied into a Linux image
# produces binaries that cannot run. `npm ci` in the build stage is what is
# wanted, and it needs package-lock.json, not the installed tree.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
# A host build output would shadow the one the image builds, so the image could
# ship a stale bundle that no build step in the Dockerfile ever produced.
web/dist/
web/coverage/
web/playwright-report/
web/test-results/
# web/.env.local deserves its own line: Vite INLINES VITE_* values from it at
# build time, so a host copy would bake this machine's deployment coordinates
# into the bundle — which is exactly what `npm run dist:check` refuses (WEB10 /
# ADR 0020). Excluding it is why that check passes inside the image on a laptop
# where it fails on the host.
web/.env.local

# ---- 3. WEIGHT: large or irrelevant trees ----------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.venv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
var/
logs/
knowledge/depgraph-snapshots/
docs/plan/
SDLC-Docs/
**/.DS_Store
